        <briefdescription>
<para>Runs the example entry point. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Invokes the example function and reports the execution status.</para><para>Runs the DMA core test. It sets up the DMA engine to receive and send packets, transmits a packet, and verifies it after loopback reception.</para><para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if the example finishes successfully, or XST_FAILURE if the example fails.</para><simplesectsep/><para>XST_SUCCESS if Example finished successfully, or XST_FAILURE if Example failed.</para></simplesect>
Runs the interrupt example test. It does the following:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Set up the output terminal if UART16550 is in the hardware build</para></listitem><listitem><para>Initialize the DMA engine</para></listitem><listitem><para>Set up Tx and Rx channels</para></listitem><listitem><para>Set up the interrupt system for the Tx and Rx interrupts</para></listitem><listitem><para>Submit a transfer</para></listitem><listitem><para>Wait for the transfer to finish</para></listitem><listitem><para>Check transfer status</para></listitem><listitem><para>Disable Tx and Rx interrupts</para></listitem><listitem><para>Print test status and exit</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if Test passed, or XST_FAILURE if Test failed.</para></simplesect>
Runs the DMA core test. It sets up DMA engine to be ready to receive and send packets, then a packet is transmitted and will be verified after it is received via the DMA loopback widget.</para><para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if Test passed, or XST_FAILURE if Test failed.</para></simplesect>
Runs the interrupt example test. It does the following: Set up the output terminal if UART16550 is in the hardware build Initialize the DMA engine Set up Tx and Rx channels Set up the interrupt system for the Tx and Rx interrupts Submit a transfer Wait for the transfer to finish Check transfer status Disable Tx and Rx interrupts Print test status and exit</para><para><simplesect kind="return"><para>XST_SUCCESS if Example finished successfully, or XST_FAILURE if Example failed. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
